{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04AY", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-codirected-limits}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:84ddc82fcbf1cb498e0874b72dfd4b0f0c3d5def1dd229a61d74b8c05caaa95a", "source_text": "Cofiltered limits", "source_text_hash": "sha256:84663635a7a46bbb1d488257c8293bc53a30d7bf7491170988d9f34bb24a55a0", "unit_id": "tag:04AY:title"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04AY", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5be071cc0ddb2a2a68aa681fc443e96d3be0d2d93104044885243e51a4b7e34e", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nLimits are easier to compute or describe when they\nare over a cofiltered diagram. Here is the definition.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6ae96ef3010e9a5819e5e85c4799c138dc46d72f4fe2c8fb4f88b685d6b521ed", "unit_id": "tag:04AY:paragraph-0001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04AY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$M : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0003": "$x, y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0005": "$z$", "MATH_0006": "$z \\to x$", "MATH_0007": "$z \\to y$", "MATH_0008": "$x, y$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0010": "$a, b : x \\to y$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0012": "$c : w \\to x$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0014": "$M(a \\circ c) = M(b \\circ c)$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0017": "$\\text{id} : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0018": "$M$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0004": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0004": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-codirected}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6800ab4a403de6cce12d27d324b1f4cae0c35f7dc468239286774512cbb971b5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e7b63b336dd2815668f5df51fbccb0b379252743ad237762b22d8deff73780c9", "source_text": "We say that a diagram <MATH_0001> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>codirected<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nor <TEXTITOPEN_0002>cofiltered<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if the following conditions hold:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the category <MATH_0002> has at least one object,\n<STRUCT_0003> for every pair of objects <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004>\nthere exist an object <MATH_0005> and morphisms <MATH_0006>,\n<MATH_0007>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> for every pair of objects <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009>\nand every pair of morphisms <MATH_0010> of <MATH_0011>\nthere exists a morphism <MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013>\nsuch that <MATH_0014> as morphisms in <MATH_0015>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nWe say that an index category <MATH_0016> is <TEXTITOPEN_0003>codirected<TEXTITCLOSE_0003>, or\n<TEXTITOPEN_0004>cofiltered<TEXTITCLOSE_0004> if <MATH_0017> is\ncofiltered (in other words you erase the <MATH_0018> in part (3) above).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:82d3e876f5ca3ccbf10968d019781e0eb00835f7d78b98815fd6cebacb6b9539", "unit_id": "tag:04AZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04AY", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-nonempty-limit}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2ad58e5c166026f4705fb86739be7ab21c9f6a301165aed9e18c88e913774c4d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe observe that any diagram with cofiltered index category is cofiltered,\nand this is how this situation usually occurs.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nAs an example of why cofiltered limits of sets are ``easier'' than\ngeneral ones, we mention the fact that a cofiltered diagram of finite\nnonempty sets has nonempty limit (Lemma <REF_0001>).\nThis result does not hold for a general limit of finite\nnonempty sets.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b262e3a22d8617d85b742509f2de23e3d62b538a05662da858dca933032bf20e", "unit_id": "tag:04AY:prose-0002"}
